# Document storage (local uploads)
#
# Anchored on purpose, and never as a bare "storage/". A .gitignore pattern
# with no slash except a trailing one matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth, so a bare "storage/" also matched backend/app/core/storage/ — the
# StorageBackend protocol and its local implementation, which app/api/deps.py
# imports. Those four files were silently never committed, and a fresh clone
# could not import the app at all: CI was the first clean checkout this project
# ever had, and it failed on exactly that (conftest ImportError, pytest exit 4).
# backend/.dockerignore already documents this hazard for the image build; the
# same reasoning belongs here.
backend/storage/
